cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the generated conversations, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "LLM Spoken Conversation: generation architecture vs. prompting in simulated telephone calls"
abstract: >-
  600 telephone conversations simulated with open LLMs (Vicuna-13B, Mistral-7B) under four
  generation architectures and three prompts, compared with the Switchboard corpus on turn
  length, coordination markers, dialogue-act structure and conceptual alignment. Generating
  the whole conversation at once is closest to human structure; giving each speaker its own
  agent moves it further away, and every setup lacks the listener behaviour that makes up a
  quarter of human talk.
